[{:db/id "q-95689/selection/c768e82240fef330252b79ca163a8555937e1f999acabf9a83c22ca9d09d3108" :answer/id #uuid "805a929d-1376-529b-a9cf-a8bfb8187ab4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{e}^{2x}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95689/selection/a55e703517843aa954965516b20694c3b80eb09b56f761ee2b5b414395e7a67a" :answer/id #uuid "f08d239f-7515-50fd-a4ca-e3b033353984" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{2x}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95689/selection/e1d3c87c13c76512ce79cfd1be46e302c6d4d1d34205d903c826163ad435edf1" :answer/id #uuid "78892773-f66a-5642-8f4e-7193c730fa52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{e}^{x}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95689/selection/9783ac592299cb0884d8b9aa43d96013de8cace0406b45f4f78ef4c5eb1398af" :answer/id #uuid "22639c2a-99d4-56c6-8f7b-345921c76974" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{e}^{2x}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95689/selection/fa942bb307437eb84e1b5897eacec994370ef8d9f8125e17082ce138aff46942" :answer/id #uuid "79b5d26e-d826-5762-befb-9c6cac781a3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95689/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d00a9ef1-3fed-5b2b-a870-3f1e2d688206" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95689/selection/e1d3c87c13c76512ce79cfd1be46e302c6d4d1d34205d903c826163ad435edf1" :answer-field/choices ["q-95689/selection/c768e82240fef330252b79ca163a8555937e1f999acabf9a83c22ca9d09d3108" "q-95689/selection/a55e703517843aa954965516b20694c3b80eb09b56f761ee2b5b414395e7a67a" "q-95689/selection/e1d3c87c13c76512ce79cfd1be46e302c6d4d1d34205d903c826163ad435edf1" "q-95689/selection/9783ac592299cb0884d8b9aa43d96013de8cace0406b45f4f78ef4c5eb1398af" "q-95689/selection/fa942bb307437eb84e1b5897eacec994370ef8d9f8125e17082ce138aff46942"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95689" :question/id #uuid "1cc17f63-e50c-556b-8900-7b2cf2330aa9" :question/math-academy-id "q-95689" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic cosine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${e}^{2x}={({e}^{x})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u={e}^{x}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{{({e}^{x})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{e}^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-95689/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "25d92a33-95e8-5860-b461-8291dac502d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95689"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95852/selection/88756ae833702bd928ba9a6cae52fdab57fb962ed64e3949375ee70863b9267e" :answer/id #uuid "70ec86c4-2d0e-5111-bd64-944071d3aea2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95852/selection/9c4ce52f1575ddc00b4afd4a3a58b743588d19cf06e023ba975cf38e918aaa29" :answer/id #uuid "c18c5c11-1fb8-5a40-97aa-db605cff8b5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95852/selection/d5c9f011e6af098ee3bf4f6847fd705010f434f08d2655d3a6f24c849e735685" :answer/id #uuid "5e5a756d-8edd-5bed-b027-235403d859a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95852/selection/284b52e1a17d7aabf71dcc2ef69f38101b8f568911c5f83c458a1a13f63ed5ef" :answer/id #uuid "1b6b538c-5cd6-5014-bf3d-9088dd407610" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95852/selection/51339b51359867ce252727f79d41927bb951d2132d1d9764e74a1f139ae45635" :answer/id #uuid "13a714cb-376f-51e3-bcd5-7006f4f8b2c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95852/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "50d08cb4-7667-5c0a-91c0-046da47555d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95852/selection/88756ae833702bd928ba9a6cae52fdab57fb962ed64e3949375ee70863b9267e" :answer-field/choices ["q-95852/selection/88756ae833702bd928ba9a6cae52fdab57fb962ed64e3949375ee70863b9267e" "q-95852/selection/9c4ce52f1575ddc00b4afd4a3a58b743588d19cf06e023ba975cf38e918aaa29" "q-95852/selection/d5c9f011e6af098ee3bf4f6847fd705010f434f08d2655d3a6f24c849e735685" "q-95852/selection/284b52e1a17d7aabf71dcc2ef69f38101b8f568911c5f83c458a1a13f63ed5ef" "q-95852/selection/51339b51359867ce252727f79d41927bb951d2132d1d9764e74a1f139ae45635"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95852" :question/id #uuid "bf611d2f-e981-5172-9028-3aadb77e03fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-95852" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-16}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-16}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic cosine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{4}.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=4\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-16}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-95852/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "25d92a33-95e8-5860-b461-8291dac502d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95852"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95861/selection/df3aa4dcb056af9fe14fc585f6ab43246cf36d53bc53db057699ded46c9e7d6c" :answer/id #uuid "e0187173-3def-55d2-944e-faafe3131d2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95861/selection/5e97593797a4411ce4095f4f412898efcc88a291b006a0deeca204d6c4453688" :answer/id #uuid "25ae9629-bba3-585e-9c97-44a26b563190" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{artanh}⁡9x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95861/selection/377d3e106da290577f6f9f3ffe048a0cd079ebcd1ed2881672d6b243533e4fb0" :answer/id #uuid "eef343b1-105f-5162-8a40-15409cd4083e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95861/selection/909faf94b2ecdab178bee23bb9e324a40484a98160c0501afe7aba71d09ec8c7" :answer/id #uuid "035f4c43-6a04-5c0c-a52c-855d2dbec9ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{artanh}⁡3x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95861/selection/44b86d16412242b80a3ec26c6803ea22d3cdf35200d473c2fee9f9b77f185313" :answer/id #uuid "bf0bceb5-7701-56a9-8aff-1e53a7c45008" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{artanh}⁡9x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95861/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "029b2f45-bd43-55bf-b8dd-3185e603ad55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95861/selection/909faf94b2ecdab178bee23bb9e324a40484a98160c0501afe7aba71d09ec8c7" :answer-field/choices ["q-95861/selection/df3aa4dcb056af9fe14fc585f6ab43246cf36d53bc53db057699ded46c9e7d6c" "q-95861/selection/5e97593797a4411ce4095f4f412898efcc88a291b006a0deeca204d6c4453688" "q-95861/selection/377d3e106da290577f6f9f3ffe048a0cd079ebcd1ed2881672d6b243533e4fb0" "q-95861/selection/909faf94b2ecdab178bee23bb9e324a40484a98160c0501afe7aba71d09ec8c7" "q-95861/selection/44b86d16412242b80a3ec26c6803ea22d3cdf35200d473c2fee9f9b77f185313"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95861" :question/id #uuid "a6accc57-b07f-5510-94f9-9ac61facd7d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-95861" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{3}{1-9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $9{x}^{2}=(3x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{1-9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{1-(3x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{artanh}⁡3x+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that this result is subject to the condition $|3x|<1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95861/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5aabe1c9-7a37-5b34-893f-9338f5c7c69a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95861"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95883/selection/c253403ff165f3549251bd7665fd818248996831694ebfb02b947020c5217f96" :answer/id #uuid "d2a33444-8144-5776-b2bb-0cb602dd17f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{1}{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95883/selection/0f8a6118a4af3da36c38ff3cc28d45234c6906cfae064f8ada3a192229792f8e" :answer/id #uuid "f33b98f8-704d-550d-94e6-3ae2732ceb0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95883/selection/7fb980972c4bf04970154dc6665451adcae16de6fad3fba398ba7fd98daee8ad" :answer/id #uuid "1edc33de-5d8c-5e45-b509-c8ae038c4f68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{1}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95883/selection/6abd64059d3db67a29e8727e6341d28887d588df561a0beefd2d7f849eab24ab" :answer/id #uuid "b687ecca-57d2-50b6-ba5c-80b00c28c5ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{1}{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95883/selection/2a08c0886afc388726ec7126774e474a6bbee593b237c6bfaa0a170aa6c73f11" :answer/id #uuid "effcfe11-e46c-5761-979b-61c1beacb738" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95883/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "20af7538-411f-5514-ad23-24a32a255af7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95883/selection/c253403ff165f3549251bd7665fd818248996831694ebfb02b947020c5217f96" :answer-field/choices ["q-95883/selection/c253403ff165f3549251bd7665fd818248996831694ebfb02b947020c5217f96" "q-95883/selection/0f8a6118a4af3da36c38ff3cc28d45234c6906cfae064f8ada3a192229792f8e" "q-95883/selection/7fb980972c4bf04970154dc6665451adcae16de6fad3fba398ba7fd98daee8ad" "q-95883/selection/6abd64059d3db67a29e8727e6341d28887d588df561a0beefd2d7f849eab24ab" "q-95883/selection/2a08c0886afc388726ec7126774e474a6bbee593b237c6bfaa0a170aa6c73f11"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95883" :question/id #uuid "280f0812-dc1a-57cc-8ada-d4af8d29cbec" :question/math-academy-id "q-95883" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{2}{1-9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{2}{1-9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{1}{1-(3x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $(3x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{1}{1-9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{1}{1-(3x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/4}\\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1/4}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1-{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{1}{4})-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{1}{4})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-95883/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd13fafc-d765-5e44-aa5a-79c2fff71212"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95883"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346522/field-1/2b7b8ca76ca5f71be01af6bf2dafd60fe370b9a92873e80d2c7d8ec849ad0007" :answer/id #uuid "03ce8b69-a178-5bce-9f24-76b01c0c8615" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\ln(2+\\sqrt{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346522/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "981baf1d-c3e3-5884-8c17-781894d4c162" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346522/field-1/2b7b8ca76ca5f71be01af6bf2dafd60fe370b9a92873e80d2c7d8ec849ad0007" :answer-field/choices ["q-346522/field-1/2b7b8ca76ca5f71be01af6bf2dafd60fe370b9a92873e80d2c7d8ec849ad0007"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346522" :question/id #uuid "163f3213-d2ff-59ff-ac09-5c275911ad5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-346522" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+9}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+9}}\\,\\text{d}x=4{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse hyperbolic sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{3}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=3\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+9}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\cdot (3\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =12{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}} \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2-12\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡0 \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2 \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+1}) \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\sqrt{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-346522/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd13fafc-d765-5e44-aa5a-79c2fff71212"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346522"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
